WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.020
After the advent of fire, three powerful souls were claimed by those who came from the dark.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.100
First was claimed by Nito, first of the dead.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.480
The second went to the Witch, who fell to the flame.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.680
And the last went to Gwyn, Lord of Sunlight.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:25.200
But there was a fourth soul, discovered afterward and hidden from the Lords: the Dark Soul.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.900
And so, the first human was furtive and kept his soul a secret.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:40.620
Lord Gwyn used his Lord Soul to usher in an age of fire and light, appointing four trusted knights to defend the realm.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.280
There was Dragonslayer Ornstein, captain of the guard.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.840
Hawkeye Gough, unmatched with a greatbow.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.140
Ciaran the Assassin, who laid waste to Gywn's enemies.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.940
And Artorias the Abysswalker.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:05.420
But in time, the flame began to fade, the Age of the Lords was ending, and the Dark Age of Men was to begin.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:15.600
"The Four Kings were powerful men. Only, their hearts were weak.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:26.460
When an evil serpent dangled the art of Lifedrain before them, they were unable to resist, and became pawns of evil."

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:36.160
The serpent in question was Darkstalker Kaathe, who tempted the Kings with the ability to drain humanity as a reward for their service.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.400
This is the art of Lifedrain.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:45.800
Kaathe's ultimate goal seems to be to return all humanity to the Abyss, as every fragment of humanity is a piece of the mighty Dark Soul.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:56.260
The knights of New Londo were transformed into Darkwraiths, beings that plagued the citizens of the city for humanity, so that it may be returned to the Abyss.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:03.020
"The Darkwraiths are the enemies of man, and any living thing that has a soul.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:13.220
They were born in New Londo, and that is where they perished; the entire city was sacrificed to contain them.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:17.060
For that is how great a threat they were."

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:45.380
As the First Flame continues to fade and with the darkness looming, the deities of Anor Londo begin to leave the doomed kingdom.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.540
Meanwhile, the Abyss breaks out again, this time in Oolacile.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:59.620
With time running out, Lord Gwyn's final command is for Artorias to halt the inevitable spread of the Abyss and to rescue Princess Dusk.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:08.340
An old man afraid of the dark, Lord Gwyn kindles the First Flame with his own soul, artificially extending his Age of Fire.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:17.400
And so, hundreds of years before the birth of the Choosen Undead, Knight Artorias and Sif meet the threat building in Oolacile.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.540
However, they do not succeed.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:33.700
"Knight Artorias came to stop this, but such a hero has nary a murmur of Dark.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:39.820
Without doubt, he will be swallowed by the Abyss, overcome by its utter blackness.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.560
Indeed, the Abyss may be unstoppable..."

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.000
"This may strike thine ear as somewhat peculiar, but...

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:04.800
Long ago, in my homeland of Oolacile, I was beset by a creature from the Abyss.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:10.560
I would have perished then, were it not for the great knight Artorias.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:17.080
In truth, I saw little of what transpired, for mine senses were already fled!

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:26.000
But even still, there was something about Artorias... A certain balance of the humours...

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.380
That quite perfectly fits your semblance.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.820
Heavens, could it be that...

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.940
So, it is thou who rescueth me?

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.160
Beset by the Abyss, the final act of Artorias was to protect his companion.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:57.080
He shielded Sif with power of his greatshield, for his arm was broken and he can no longer bear the burden.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:04.260
Soon after, the spread of the Abyss was halted, and the deeds of a human were accredited to Artorias.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.260
The hero who gave his life to repel the Abyss.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:15.120
Within this glimpse of the Abyss, lies a tormented soul, the savior turned demon, hidden from the eyes of his lord and comrades.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.400
As if only for his soul to find peace at long last, a warrior came.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.040
A hero of a time long distant yet near.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:29.700
The warrior fought against Artorias, severing his bonds with the darkness, so that his honour may remain intact.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:40.380
Living with the knowledge that his master saved him with his last uncorrupted breath, watching him become husk, only capable of demented screams.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:47.800
He keeps the ring of Artorias, knowing that many will try to traverse the Abyss and defends his master's grave.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:54.080
Imagine what he is feeling when you come to him years later for the abyss walker ring that debilitated his friend

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.920
He is trying to protect you.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:02.400
One of you will have to die, because Sif will not give you the Covenant of Artorias willingly.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.160
Maybe in death, he can find his friend Artorias again.

